---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema, articleSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { helpers } from '../../lib/helpers';
const lang = 'en';
const h = helpers();
const { E, F, P, pc, pp, wk, num, gb } = h;
const meta = F.META_DATA;
const YL = h.yearLabel(h.lastYear);
const ML = h.month(h.lastMonth);
const hen = h.C('hendon-london');
const ex = E.odds((E.rate(E.centre('hendon-london')) as number) / 100, 17, 'f');
const cost = E.licenceCost({ hours: 30, price: 38, passRate: (E.rate(E.centre('hendon-london')) as number) / 100, theoryRate: gb.theory, evening: false, licence: 'online' });
const s = (k: Parameters<typeof h.src>[0], t?: string) => h.src(k, t);
// Months whose median wait repeats the previous month at most centres: reproduced as published, flagged here.
const allMonths = [...new Set(F.FULL_CENTRES.flatMap((c) => Object.keys(c.wait)))].sort();
const repeats = allMonths.slice(1).map((m, i) => { const p = allMonths[i]; const both = F.FULL_CENTRES.filter((c) => c.wait[m] && c.wait[p]); return { m, p, n: both.filter((c) => c.wait[m][0] === c.wait[p][0]).length, of: both.length }; }).filter((x) => x.of && x.n / x.of > 0.5);
---
<PageLayout title="Driving Test Data Method: DVSA Tables, Estimates and Limits" description="How Test Centre Pass Rates builds each driving test centre record from DVSA tables: pass rates, waits, nearby centres, distances, three estimates and limits." lang={lang} jsonLd={[articleSchema({ title: 'How the driving test centre figures are built', description: 'Method of Test Centre Pass Rates', path: route('method', lang), lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Method', path: route('method', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Method' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><p class="kicker">Method</p><h1 class="mt-1 text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">How the driving test centre figures are built</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <p>Every page and every tool reads the same files, generated by one script, <code>scripts/update-data.py</code>, from the DVSA statistical data set <Fragment set:html={s('dvsa_data', 'Driving test and theory test data: cars')} />. No rate or wait is typed into a page. The DVSA page was last updated on {displayDate(meta.statsPageUpdated, 'en-GB')} and the tables were read on {displayDate(meta.retrieved, 'en-GB')}. A scheduled job runs the script on the 16th of every month and rebuilds the site when a table has changed.</p>
    <h2>1. Pass rates by centre</h2>
    <p>Table DRT122A gives, for each car practical test centre and each financial year (April to March), the tests conducted and the passes, by sex. The site keeps five years, {h.yearLabel(F.years(F.full('hendon-london'))[0])} to {YL}; the pass rate is passes divided by tests. DRT122C adds first attempts, first-attempt passes and passes with no driving fault; DRT122D the tests and passes by age from 17 to 25; DRT122E automatic cars; DRT122B the tests cancelled by DVSA, by reason. The {YL} tables were published on {displayDate(meta.passRatesUpdated, 'en-GB')}. Hendon, for instance, conducted {num(hen.tests)} tests and recorded {num(hen.passes)} passes: {pc(hen.rate)}.</p>
    <p>A centre is shown when it appears in DRT122A for {YL} and in the waiting table within its last six months. {meta.skipped.length} names of the tables are left out because the centre closed, moved or only tests lorries; their tests remain in the national totals. DVSA withholds figures where one examiner did all the tests of a category, shown as "n/a".</p>
    <h2>2. Waiting times</h2>
    <p>DRT122F gives, for each centre and month of test, the median number of weeks between the booking and the test, the weeks it took for the first 10 % of that month's tests to be booked, the share booked within seven weeks and the share of slots left free. The site keeps 24 months, to {ML} (DVSA update of {meta.waitsUpdated}). National and regional figures come from DRT121G: in {ML} the median wait in Great Britain was {wk(gb.wait?.[3])}. A median wait describes tests already taken; it is not the date a booking made today would get.{repeats.map((x) => ` In the file DVSA published, the median wait for ${h.month(x.m)} is identical to ${h.month(x.p)} at ${num(x.n)} of ${num(x.of)} centres, while the other columns differ${(() => { const G = E.NATIONAL.areas['Great Britain'] as Record<string, number[]>; return G[x.m] && G[x.p] && G[x.m][3] === G[x.p][3] ? ', and the national table DRT121G repeats the same median for Great Britain' : ''; })()}; the site reproduces the figures as published and will take DVSA's correction when it appears.`).join('')}</p>
    <h2>3. Addresses, nearby centres and distances</h2>
    <p>Addresses and test types are those of the <Fragment set:html={s('gov_find_centre', 'GOV.UK centre finder')} />. The three centres a test can be moved to are those of DVSA's <Fragment set:html={s('gov_nearest', 'list of nearest centres')} />, which applies since {h.date(P.rules.nearestThreeFrom)}; their mileage is DVSA's. Every other distance is a straight line between British National Grid positions: the centre's postcode, and the centre of the postcode district you type, both from <Fragment set:html={s('os_codepoint', 'Ordnance Survey Code-Point Open')} />. Road distances are longer.</p>
    <h2>4. National figures</h2>
    <p>DRT121A gives the national pass rate by year since 2007/08 and by quarter, DRT121C by age and sex, DRT121D by attempt number, DRT121F the most common serious faults. In {YL}: {pc(gb.rate)} overall, {pc(gb.f)} for women, {pc(gb.m)} for men, {pc(E.attemptRate(1))} at a first attempt and {pc(E.attemptRate(6))} at a sixth or later. Theory tests by centre come from DRT112A ({E.THEORY_CENTRES.length} centres, {pc(gb.theory)} in Great Britain).</p>
    <h2>5. The three estimates</h2>
    <p><strong>Chance by age and sex at one centre.</strong> DVSA does not publish centre rates by age and sex together. The estimate multiplies the centre's {YL} rate by the ratio between the national rate of that age and sex and the national rate of all candidates. For a woman of 17 at Hendon: {pp(E.rate(E.centre('hendon-london')))} × {num(Math.round(ex.factor * 100))} % = {pc(ex.p)}. It assumes a centre's routes affect every group alike.</p>
    <p><strong>Chance of passing within a number of attempts.</strong> Each attempt uses the centre rate scaled by the national rate of that attempt number (DRT121D), attempts treated as independent. Real candidates who fail often take more lessons first, so this is a rough guide.</p>
    <p><strong>Cost of a licence.</strong> Lessons are the hours and the hourly price you type; DVSA publishes no average number of hours, so none is assumed. The <Fragment set:html={s('gov_adi_survey', 'DVSA instructor survey')} /> of October 2025 ({num(P.adiSurvey.responses)} answers) found {P.adiSurvey.bands[3].pc} % of instructors charging £36 to £40 an hour; that range sets the default price. Theory and practical fees (£{P.fees.theory}, £{P.fees.practicalWeekday} or £{P.fees.practicalEvening}, <Fragment set:html={s('gov_cost', 'GOV.UK')} />) are multiplied by the expected number of attempts, one divided by the pass rate. The provisional licence costs £{P.fees.provisionalOnline} online (<Fragment set:html={s('gov_provisional', 'GOV.UK')} />). Thirty hours at £38 with a test at Hendon: {h.m(cost.total)}.</p>
    <h2>6. Tests</h2>
    <p>On every build: the sum of the centre tables for {YL} must stay within 2 % of the national total of DRT121A (DVSA leaves a few single-examiner centres out of the centre tables); Hendon's {YL} figures are checked against the published table; distances are checked on known pairs; every estimate stays between 1 % and 99 %; every page passes the editorial checks. A failing test stops the build.</p>
    <h2>7. What the site does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Northern Ireland: tests there are run by the Driver and Vehicle Agency (<Fragment set:html={s('ni_dva', 'nidirect')} />), whose figures are not in the DVSA tables.</li>
      <li>Lorry, bus, motorcycle and instructor tests, which DVSA publishes in other tables.</li>
      <li>Test routes, which DVSA does not publish, and live slot availability, which only the GOV.UK booking service shows.</li>
      <li>Booking, moving or cancelling a test, or alerting you to a cancellation: that is done only on <Fragment set:html={s('gov_book', 'GOV.UK')} />.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Method version: {LAST_UPDATED}. A figure that looks wrong: <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact</a>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
